## Resolution

Implemented `nrl.model/0` and the `nrl.feed-forward` adapter: a bounded stateless graph of affine/gated/SiLU/ReLU/add operations with explicit shared objects, checked aliases, scalar f64 policy and activation limits. Complete standalone models and exact-base replacement overlays preserve source declarations, licences/notices and change history; resolving an overlay removes its runtime base dependency. SHA-256 binds graph, object bytes and profile/metadata without claiming authenticity. CLI commands package, inspect, execute and export these artifacts, refuse existing outputs and report the written model's identity.

At `fed14350`, **44 Rust host tests** (seven model tests), both portable release rlibs, the 12-case numerical demonstration, five-representation QSL bridge and full model CLI cycle passed on the NRL branch. External PyTorch graphs cover all five gated representations, rectangular affine layers, explicit shared objects and an ordinary independent affine/ReLU/affine network. The affine primitive also matches external autograd and independent central differences. The six fixture files regenerate byte-identically. [Machine-readable evidence](../nrl/reports/model-graph-2026-10-26.json), [raw log](../nrl/reports/model-check-2026-10-26.txt), [format and limits](../nrl/specs/model-v0.md).

The code is built and staged into fast-test without tests there; the full repository gate and main integration belong to the deferred landing round. T05's dataset/task/training pipeline, QSL whole-language-model import, other family adapters and T11 native integration remain open under 900. No quality, measured compression/speedup or native-platform guarantee is claimed.
